 4. ⚡ Military preps for new Iran strikes 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A sailor runs down the flight deck of the USS George Washington in the Arabian Sea last month. Photo: Ed Ou/Reuters Intel from Axios' Barak Ravid: The Pentagon instructed U.S. Central Command several days ago to be ready to resume major combat operations in Iran.

 Why it matters: The directive didn't include a specific date for launching strikes, and President Trump hasn't made any final decisions. But U.S. and Israeli sources say it could happen before the U.S. midterm elections and possibly the Israeli elections a week earlier. If major combat operations resume, they're expected to include massive bombing of Iranian energy, infrastructure and nuclear targets, sources say.

 Trump's national security team met at Camp David for several hours on Friday to discuss the war and other issues. An Israeli official told Axios that part of the meeting focused on a possible resumption of major combat operations in Iran. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said after the meeting that it focused on "long-term" foreign policy planning. 👀 Behind the scenes: President Trump spoke yesterday with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. It was their second call in days, after barely speaking for many weeks.

 The call took place after Netanyahu held a meeting with his national security team about Iran, the first Israeli official said. Share this story . 

 
 
