 5. 🇺🇦 Mapped: Ukraine&#x27;s counterpunch 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: ISW . Map: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals A Ukrainian counteroffensive over the past few weeks has forced Russian forces back in several pockets along the front line and undercut Moscow's narrative that it will control all of the eastern Donbas region, Axios' Dave Lawler writes. 

 Why it matters: The gains are more symbolically significant than territorial. After years of grinding warfare in which relatively little land has changed hands, even modest shifts in momentum carry outsized weight. Mapped : Ukraine claws back land, thwarting a Russian push (NYT). 

 
 
