 7. 📺 Election night &quot;nerd show&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Anthony Salvanto in 2024. Photo: CBS News CBS News is launching a new election night streaming show that lets political junkies watch its decision desk analyze races and make calls in real time, Axios Media Trends author Sara Fischer writes. 

 Why it matters: "The Nerd Show" represents the network's first election-focused show built for a digital audience. How it works: The special streaming show will begin at 5 p.m. ET, a few hours before CBS News' official election broadcast.

 It'll be hosted by CBS News executive director of elections and surveys Anthony Salvanto alongside congressional correspondent Caitlin Huey-Burns. The big touchscreen map will be branded "The Hub." Share this story . 

 Ross Douthat (left) interviews retiring Sen. Thom Tillis (R-N.C.) on last Sunday's "60 Minutes." Photo: CBS News Scoop: I've learned that Ross Douthat — the former New York Times columnist who became a "60 Minutes" correspondent — will write a weekly column for The Free Press . 

 Bari Weiss, editor-in-chief of CBS News and founder of The Free Press ("for free people"), has driven synergies between the two organizations, both owned by Skydance. 
 
